WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.060
With so many new shows premiering, it's a
pretty competitive field, but these debuting

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:10.070
series have captivated audiences and critics
alike so from streaming gems to big network

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:13.980
efforts, here are the very best TV shows of
2019.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.580
Natasha Lyonne has been a Hollywood fixture
for years, and when critics and audiences

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.520
heard she would be creating her own show,
they paid attention.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.420
As Nadia, a woman stuck in a bizarre time
loop where she keeps reliving her death on

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.789
her birthday with absolutely no explanation
or context, Lyonne inhabits the role with

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:32.100
caustic wit and razor-sharp timing.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.400
Along the way, she meets Alan, played by Charlie
Barnett, who is stuck in his own terrifying

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.160
time loop.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.440
"Hey man, didn't you get the news, we’re
about to die."

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.880
"It doesn’t matter I die all the time."

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:50.160
Together, the two of them work together to
avoid death, solve their seemingly unsolvable

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.980
problems, and, hopefully, track down Nadia's
missing cat, Oatmeal.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.210
The series' careful attention to detail and
Lyonne's anchoring lead performance earned

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.980
rave reviews, and so did her intense involvement
with the production.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.520
Along with starring, Lyonne directed the season
finale and came up with the concept.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.220
Though fans would certainly welcome a second
season, it ended on a rare, perfect note,

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.200
just in case it only sticks around for a single
batch of episodes.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.960
Based on the popular Dark Horse comic book
series by My Chemical Romance frontman Gerard

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:24.800
Way and artist Gabriel Bá, The Umbrella Academy
premiered in February of 2019 to plenty of

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:30.280
buzz from fans excited for a live-action adaptation
with an incredible cast led by Ellen Page.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:34.700
The strange adventure centers on seven children
with supernatural abilities who were raised

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:38.940
in a mysterious school, shifting between flashbacks
and the catastrophic problems they have in

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.300
their adult lives in the present day.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.660
"Looks like some temporal anomaly.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.900
Either that or a miniature black hole, one
of the 2.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.320
"Pretty big difference there, Paul Bunyan."

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:53.480
These children, born during a mysterious event
and given numbers by the Academy's headmaster,

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.730
Sir Reginald Hargreeves, try to suppress their
supernatural abilities.

00:01:56.730 --> 00:02:02.229
Now, as adults, they must reunite their bizarre,
broken family to prevent an oncoming apocalypse.

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:07.280
Umbrella Academy earned pretty positive reviews
from critics, and audiences clearly agreed.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.140
Netflix quickly renewed the show for a second
season, with the entire cast and creative

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.140
team returning.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:17.080
If you loved the 2014 comedy What We Do in
the Shadows, directed by Thor: Ragnarok's

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:22.000
Taika Waititi and Flight of the Conchords'
Jemaine Clement, then you'll love FX's television

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.780
adaptation, which premiered in the spring
of 2019.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.380
"Where did they find the alcohol?"

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.920
“No, they were half drunk.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.760
They’d been half drunk.”

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:30.560
“Oh…”

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.200
“Please, finish the whole victim before
moving on to the next one, okay?"

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:38.920
With a new cast and a new setting, the series
focuses on three vampires living as roommates

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:43.110
in New York City's Staten Island, which they're
also trying to conquer for the entire race

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.110
of vampires.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.970
Naturally, the trio gets into plenty of trouble,
embarking on affairs with humans and struggling

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:52.900
to assimilate even though they can only go
out in the dead of night and are all centuries

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:53.400
old.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.920
Created by Clement, who oversees the show
with Waititi, this version of Shadows naturally

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.680
shares the charming awkwardness of the original
film, employing the same bumbling, deadpan

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:06.400
humor that has characterized much of both
Clement and Waititi's work.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.860
Putting absurd characters in universal situations
has always been a calling card for both of

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:15.500
these creators, and by returning to a concept
they knew was successful and giving it new

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.340
life, they ended up with another hit.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:23.560
A Netflix original series created by cartoonist
and writer Lisa Hanawalt, the sadly short-lived

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:28.400
Tuca &amp; Bertie featured the voices of Tiffany
Haddish, Ali Wong, and Steven Yeun as the

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:28.900
core cast.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.000
The series focuses on two women struggling
to find themselves as they navigate life in

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:38.110
their 30s, dealing with anxiety, harassment
from coworkers, and serious medical issues.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.540
Also, they're birds.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.780
"Bertie is the best bird in the whole world.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:46.090
She could kick your ass and we’re having
a really big fight right now but she’s my

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.090
best friend."

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:52.300
Tuca, a toucan, is outspoken and brash, constantly
struggling to hold down a job as well as managing

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:57.349
her sobriety; Bertie, a songbird, takes her
career in an office extremely seriously but

00:03:57.349 --> 00:03:58.849
dreams of being a baker.

00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:03.120
And Speckle, a robin and Bertie's fairly uptight
boyfriend, works as an architect.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:08.220
With a recurring cast rounded out by comedians
and actors like Awkwafina, Tessa Thompson,

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:12.209
and even Isabella Rosselini, the show received
glowing reviews from critics.

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:14.920
Unfortunately, that didn't seal the deal for
Netflix.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.820
In July of 2019, Tuca &amp; Bertie was cancelled.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.199
Fans and critics alike bemoaned the decision,
especially after it turned out that Netflix

00:04:22.199 --> 00:04:25.949
may not have given it a fair shot, thanks
to an algorithm that didn't even recommend

00:04:25.949 --> 00:04:27.200
the show to Hanawalt herself.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:31.980
At the very least, though, we all have one
perfect season of Tuca &amp; Bertie to enjoy over

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:32.880
and over again.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:36.860
It may be too late to get the show another
season, but it's not too late for you to discover

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:37.540
its charm.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:42.300
Even though many historical dramas across
film and television focus on truly horrific

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:46.490
events, there are still stories that need
to be retold in new ways, and that's especially

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.260
true of HBO's Chernobyl.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:51.979
Though most people have a passing familiarity
with the nuclear disaster that struck the

00:04:51.979 --> 00:04:57.849
Soviet Union in 1986, this show goes more
in-depth than any depiction has gone before,

00:04:57.849 --> 00:05:02.439
creating a difficult, upsetting, and altogether
necessary experience for viewers.

00:05:02.439 --> 00:05:07.550
The show stars Mad Men's Jared Harris as Valery
Legasov, a real-life director at a scientific

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:12.479
institute that tried to clean up after the
unprecedented and catastrophic nuclear explosion.

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:17.050
Chernobyl contains plenty of staggering moments,
from attempts to cover up the explosion and

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:21.939
its cause, to a truly harrowing episode where
soldiers and veterans must hunt down household

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:25.780
pets left behind after the evacuation to prevent
further contamination.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:29.420
"They're radioactive so they have to go.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:32.100
It’s not hard they’re mostly pets.”

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:36.560
The most upsetting story of all might be that
of the firefighters who were the first to

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.229
respond to the disaster, and who suffered
a horrifying fate from the effects of radiation.

00:05:41.229 --> 00:05:45.020
The difficult and extremely faithful efforts
that the cast and crew put in to the series

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:45.660
were worth it.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:50.800
The show was met with universal adoration
and received several nominations for the 2019

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.180
Emmy Awards, including one for Harris and
one for Outstanding Limited Series.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.740
In this day and age, it's more important than
ever for television and film to depict different

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:04.249
perspectives as often as possible, which is
perfectly on display in Hulu's Ramy.

00:06:04.249 --> 00:06:08.530
A half-hour comedy with a healthy amount of
dramatic elements, the show was created by

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:09.960
its star, Ramy Youssef.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.880
As a first-generation American Muslim who
must figure out how to balance his religious

00:06:13.889 --> 00:06:18.869
background and family against the modern millennial
landscape, the show brings a shared experience

00:06:18.869 --> 00:06:24.330
for many Muslim Americans to life with heart,
humor, sharp writing, and an anchoring performance

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:25.020
by Youssef.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:29.960
From finding a place in American society in
the continued aftermath of 9/11, to navigating

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:34.229
the dating scene despite his strict Egyptian
family's reservations, the show has struck

00:06:34.229 --> 00:06:38.741
a serious chord with Muslim Americans and
critics alike, earning great reviews for the

00:06:38.741 --> 00:06:39.920
show's debut season.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:45.060
Very few shows focus on such a specific yet
universal experience, and thanks to Youssef,

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:50.120
many young people can now turn on a show that
is actually faithful to their lives, upbringings,

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.280
and experiences in a divided America.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:56.420
Luckily for Youssef and his fans, the show
has already been renewed for a second season.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:02.300
There's always room for another oddball, irreverent
comedy on television, and creator Julio Torres,

00:07:02.309 --> 00:07:06.340
a writer for Saturday Night Live who produced
some of the show's standout sketches over

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:10.089
the past few years, certainly delivered with
Los Espookys on HBO.

00:07:10.089 --> 00:07:15.210
Cowritten by Torres and Ana Fabrega, both
of whom also star, the show focuses on a group

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:19.199
of friends who want to make a business out
of their horror obsessions as they navigate

00:07:19.199 --> 00:07:23.550
life in a Latin American country riddled with
supernatural happenings that go beyond their

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.420
special effects.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:29.039
By blending absurdist humor and perfectly
dry writing with horror, Los Espookys has

00:07:29.039 --> 00:07:34.289
scored great reviews for its inaugural season,
and HBO has already renewed this spooky, kooky

00:07:34.289 --> 00:07:35.440
show for a second season.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:40.680
Eastbound &amp; Down and Vice Principals proved
that Danny McBride and HBO were a winning

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.320
combination, and fans have been eagerly awaiting
their next collaboration.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:49.720
In 2019, it arrived in the form of The Righteous
Gemstones, which McBride created in addition

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:52.840
to serving as lead actor, executive producer,
and director.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:57.780
Alongside John Goodman and Adam DeVine, McBride
plays a member of the televangelist Gemstone

00:07:57.789 --> 00:08:01.999
family, who are obviously much more corrupt
than their ultra-religious, pious exterior

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:02.620
might seem.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.900
"Everybody in your line keeps getting water
up their nose you’re tipping em back too

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:06.400
far.”

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:07.920
“Why don’t you it your way and I’ll
do it mine?”

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.320
“How about you do it right, how about that?

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.320
Watch this get over here."

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:16.539
Through various manipulations, schemes, and
fake charity projects, the family reaps their

00:08:16.539 --> 00:08:20.819
dubious rewards, constantly squabbling with
each other over control of the empire.

00:08:20.819 --> 00:08:25.529
Thanks to a talented comedic cast which also
includes Walton Goggins as the instantly iconic

00:08:25.529 --> 00:08:31.069
Baby Billy as well as its pitch-perfect writing
that lampoons the entire televangelist industry,

00:08:31.069 --> 00:08:34.410
the show has received not only great reviews,
but a second season order.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:38.600
It looks like the conniving Gemstone family
will continue to grace HBO's airwaves for

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:39.600
quite some time.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:44.960
Fans of Jim Henson's 1982 film The Dark Crystal
were thrilled when Netflix announced that

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:48.930
they were working on a prequel series to the
cult classic dark puppet saga.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:52.840
When the show finally premiered in 2019, it
didn't disappoint in the slightest.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:57.300
Just like the original film, the entire cast
is made up of stunning puppet creations from

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.400
the Henson Workshop, performed by some of
the finest puppeteers in the world and voiced

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.610
by talented actors.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:07.250
Together, they work to bring life to a story
that's equal parts fantastic wonder and political

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:09.700
drama that feels like Game of Thrones with
puppets.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:14.660
Executive produced by Henson's daughter Lisa,
the series recaptures the handmade artistry

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:19.160
of the movie while incorporating new technologies
and a stacked voice cast that includes an

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.020
amazingly varied roster of talent.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:26.900
In addition to main characters played by Taron
Egerton, Anya-Taylor Joy, and Nathalie Emmanuel,

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:33.110
the show features Lena Headey, Helena Bonham
Carter, Natalie Dormer, Andy Samberg, Awkwafina,

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:37.100
Simon Pegg, Keegan-Michael Key, and Sigourney
Weaver, just to name a few.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.320
"I've seen the dark signs.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:41.340
Strange storms.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.060
Sand where there used to be sea.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.620
Thra is dying."

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:51.480
Set in a fantastic world of magic, Age of
Resistance tells the story of three Gelfings

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:56.550
named Rian, Brea, and Deet, who discover the
horrifying intentions of their seemingly benevolent

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.060
rulers, the Skeksis.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:02.280
The ten-episode series has earned overwhelming
acclaim from critics and audiences alike,

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:06.880
who love its engrossing storyline, faithfulness
to its source material, and artful direction

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:08.080
by Louis Leterrier.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:12.220
It remains to be seen if there will be a second
season, but there's certainly more of Thra

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:12.920
to explore.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:18.140
Comedy can sometimes be a total boy's club,
so to remedy that, HBO put its full weight

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:21.940
behind a radical new sketch show, bluntly
named A Black Lady Sketch Show.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:26.280
Created by comedian Robin Thede, the former
head writer for The Nightly Show with Larry

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:30.070
Wilmore, A Black Lady Sketch Show is, well,
exactly what it sounds like.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:34.650
The sketch show features talented performers
and comedians in a variety of skits lampooning

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:37.420
the day to day life of black women in America.

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:40.920
The show has been met with plenty of love
since it premiered in the summer of 2019,

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:45.730
and was subsequently renewed by HBO for a
second season, so it looks like fans will

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:48.880
be able to get more face time with these funny
women before too long.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:53.480
Saturday Night Live might be a breeding ground
for some of the finest comedic talent around,

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:57.680
but sometimes, they decline to air some of
the weirder sketches pitched by their writers.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:02.560
Luckily for everyone, former SNL writer Tim
Robinson now has a safe haven for some of

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.660
its rejected sketches, which found a home
on his Netflix show: I Think You Should Leave.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:10.980
Produced by the Lonely Island, with Akiva
Schaffer, one third of the comedy trio, directing

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:15.280
several episodes of its first season, I Think
You Should Leave offers up some of the weirdest

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:17.780
and most delightful sketches in recent memory.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:22.880
Distant future Christmas skeletons, a car
focus group gone horribly wrong, hot dog costumes,

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:28.180
and the almost upsettingly surreal Garfield
House set the tone for hilariously weird stuff.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.540
"I'll never forget the day I told you I bought
Jim Davis’ house.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:32.840
The creator of Garfield.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:34.910
You sat there and stared at me.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:37.620
Like I didn’t just tell you that I just
bought Jim Davis's house!"

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:41.730
The overall conceit of the show is that throughout
every sketch, the characters happily accept

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:45.300
increasingly bizarre elements within normal,
everyday situations.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:49.560
Lean in along with them and enjoy the ride,
as many critics and fans have already done,

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:53.060
and remember that it's okay if you can't quite
choose which sketch is your favorite.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:57.280
Robinson and his crew aren't finished, either;
with the show returning for a second season

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:57.960
this year.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:03.840
Director Ava DuVernay made her mark with the
Academy Award-nominated Selma, and in 2019,

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:07.820
she gave Netflix one of its most prestigious
projects with the miniseries When They See

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:11.860
Us, a searing, unflinching look at the case
of the famous "Central Park Five."

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:17.040
In 1989, five young African American boys
were falsely accused of assaulting a woman

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.640
in Central Park, and imprisoned for years
despite their innocence.

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:25.910
When the actual guilty party was discovered
in 2002, he not only confessed, but was definitively

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:28.180
linked to the crime using DNA evidence.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:32.140
By then, most of the Central Park Five had
already finished their sentences, but they

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:37.550
filed suit against the city of New York, finally
winning a settlement and vindication in 2016,

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:39.810
almost two decades after their imprisonment.

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:44.250
DuVernay, who also wrote the series, directs
with a steady and sure hand, making no secret

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:48.860
of the fact that these men were the victims
of wrongful imprisonment and racial prejudice.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:52.900
With younger actors as the Five supported
by veteran performers like John Leguizamo

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:57.750
, and Niecy Nash, it's no wonder that When
They See Us earned universal acclaim, including

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.240
eleven Emmy nominations.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:04.140
There are plenty of dark comedies to choose
from right now, but don't sleep on Netflix's

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:07.300
Dead to Me, an extremely worthy entry into
this trendy genre.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:12.280
Starring two accomplished and well-known actresses,
Christina Applegate and Linda Cardellini,

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:17.680
this edgy show from comedian and writer Liz
Feldman is both exactly as funny and way darker

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:18.720
than you might expect.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:23.360
It focuses on two women who bond over their
shared widowhood and forge an extremely intense

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:23.860
friendship.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:28.240
The show is stocked with plenty of twists,
and before too long, it seems as if Judy might

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:32.990
not be who she claims, leading Jen down a
potentially dangerous and hurtful rabbit hole

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:33.900
with her new companion.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:38.560
Despite the bleak premise, the show is often
incredibly funny, letting Applegate and Cardellini

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:39.760
riff on each other.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:43.150
It doesn't hurt that there's a great supporting
cast that includes James Marsden, Ed Asner,

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:44.640
and others.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:49.100
Dead to Me was an immediate hit for Netflix,
who paid attention and renewed it for a second

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:49.600
season.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:54.780
After How I Met Your Mother ended in 2013,
Cobie Smulders, who spent nine seasons playing

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:57.840
the leading role of Robin Scherbatsky, was
plenty busy.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:02.280
Not only did she join the Marvel Cinematic
Universe, popping up frequently as Maria Hill,

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:06.680
but her next leading role arrived in 2019,
when she was finally awarded her own network

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:07.180
series.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:12.720
Based on a comic book series of the same name,
ABC's Stumptown tells the story of Dex Parios,

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:16.500
a down-and-out Marine veteran who takes up
a side hustle as a private investigator in

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.620
Portland, Oregon.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:21.940
Dex has certainly had a rough go of it not
only did her childhood sweetheart die in front

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:26.100
of her in Afghanistan, but she struggles with
gambling debts and unemployment.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:30.580
In order to boost her PI practice, she involves
her best friend Grey McConnell, a compelling

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:35.460
role for New Girl's Jake Johnson, whose shady
criminal past ends up helping Dex solve local

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:35.960
crimes.

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:40.380
She's also got some help from the police department
itself, enlisting her would-be boyfriend Detective

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:44.300
Miles Hoffman to send her cases whenever the
Portland PD needs assistance.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:49.020
During its first season, Stumptown has made
a considerable critical splash thanks to Smulders'

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:53.120
anchoring performance and clever plotting,
which echoes classic detective shows like

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.540
The Rockford Files, but updated with a very
modern sensibility.

00:14:56.720 --> 00:15:00.000
Fans can only hope it continues running on
ABC for quite some time.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:05.320
In early January of 2019, Netflix kicked off
the new year with its first critically acclaimed

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:10.100
release: Sex Education, a raucous British
teen comedy with a purposefully provocative

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:10.600
title.

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:15.040
Asa Butterfield plays the lead role of Otis,
a young boy ashamed of his own sexuality,

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:19.880
who has to deal with his mother, played by
Gillian Anderson, a prominent and pretty invasive

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:22.440
sex therapist who misguidedly wants to help
him.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:26.900
After Otis accidentally helps his bully get
past some of his own sexual inadequacies,

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:31.250
he sets up his own sex therapy practice at
school with the help of his gorgeous bad-girl

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:33.400
classmate Maeve, to great success.

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:33.900
"Therapy?"

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.640
"Yeah, sex therapy, you have a gift.

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:38.300
It would be irresponsible to waste it."

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:42.280
The show has already been renewed for a second
season after its first eight episodes premiered

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:43.160
to great acclaim.

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:47.320
Beyond great performances and a big name with
Anderson, the show was soundly praised for

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:52.460
its positive, open attitude toward sex, helping
teenage and adult viewers alike grapple with

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:57.020
their own insecurities as well as normalizing
healthy sexual behaviors and attitudes.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:16:01.720
That's an unfortunately rare perspective for
most television shows, but it's also a refreshing

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:02.220
one.

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:08.180
Based on an Israeli series of the same name,
HBO's daring teen drama Euphoria burst onto

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:13.680
the scene during the summer of 2019, balancing
over-the-top imagery with grounded performances

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.740
and alarmingly real teenage issues.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:21.180
Produced by Drake and anchored by a stunning
performance by Zendaya, Euphoria centers on

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:25.600
17-year-old Rue Bennett, a recovering drug
addict returning to school while continuing

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.360
to battle her ongoing addiction.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:32.440
Euphoria stirred up plenty of controversy
during its first season thanks to extensive

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:37.560
nicety, a graphic depiction of saxophone assault,
and its visual imaginings of teenage driving

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:38.060
trips.

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:41.740
But that didn't stop the first season from
racking up rave reviews.

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:46.510
HBO clearly believes in the show as well — before
the debut season had even concluded, they

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:48.680
picked up Euphoria for a second season.

